mage/s65-28462/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-09T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-28462 (3-7 June 1965) --- Christopher C. Kraft Jr., assistant director for Flight Operations, at his console in the Mission Control Center during Gemini-4 spaceflight.  He served as mission director and as a flight director.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-28462","photographer":"n/a","title":"MISSION CONTROL CENTER (MCC) - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 ACTIVITY - MSC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-28462/s65-28462~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":125000,"height":900},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-28462/s65-28462~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":38000,"height":450},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-28462/s65-28462~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":38000,"height":450},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-28462/s65-28462~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":277000,"height":1350},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-28462/s65-28462~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-12-07T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-30263 (3 June 1965) --- Shown at their consoles during the liftoff of Gemini-4 (from left) are astronauts Clifford C. Williams Jr., Frank Borman and Alan B. Shepard Jr.  Borman was command pilot of the backup crew for the Gemini-4 flight. The three astronauts monitored the flight from the Mission Control Center at Cape Kennedy.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-30263","photographer":"N/A","title":"MISSION CONTROL CENTER (MCC) ACTIVITY - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/s65-30263~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":130000,"height":842},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/s65-30263~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":40000,"height":421},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/s65-30263~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":40000,"height":421},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/s65-30263~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":305000,"height":1264},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-30263/s65-30263~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-52754/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-52754 (12 Sept. 1966) --- Three key Manned Spacecraft Center (MSC) officials hold discussion in the Mission Control room during Gemini-11 activity. Left to right, are Donald K. Slayton, MSC Director of Flight Crew Operations; astronaut Alan B. Shepard Jr., Chief, MSC Astronaut Office; and George M. Low, MSC Deputy Director. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ADMINISTRATION","ASTRONAUTS","CONFERENCES","FLIGHT CONTROL","GEMINI 11 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GROUND BASED CONTROL","INTEGRATED MISSION CONTROL CENTER"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-52754","title":"Three MSC officials hold discussion in Mission Control room during Gemini 11"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-52754/s66-52754~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1277,"size":180000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-52754/s66-52754~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":638,"size":49000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-52754/s66-52754~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":638,"size":49000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-52754/s66-52754~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1915,"size":432000,"height":1920},{"href":"h